        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0629" n="541" xml:id="pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4500: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-12T11:00:00-05:00">December 12, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>514. My 513, December 11, midnight. The Uruguayan Minister late last night went
                    to the office of the Associated Press to state that he had never made any such
                    statements as those transmitted by the Associated Press and quoted in my
                    telegram under reference. He requested that the story be killed. When he was
                    told that this was impossible he requested that a new statement be transmitted
                    in place of the one which he had actually previously made in which all reference
                    to myself was omitted.</p>
                <p>In view of the action taken I do not consider any statement by me necessary
                    particularly since none of the statements originally made are carried by the
                    local press for this morning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
